WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.362
A shuffle means Spark has to redistribute data between workers.

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.452
Consider grouping millions of sales records by customer.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:13.617
The records for one customer may currently be spread across many partitions.

00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:19.794
Before Spark can calculate that customer's total, those related records need to be brought together.

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:25.655
That movement uses network, memory, and sometimes disk resources.

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:31.380
Grouping, global sorting, distinct operations, and many joins can cause shuffles.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.210
A shuffle is not automatically a mistake.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.670
Sometimes it is required to answer the question.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:44.753
The goal is to recognize when it happens and avoid unnecessary movement.
